WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720
Speaker 1: We talked yesterday. We had two&nbsp;
relevant stories yesterday to what we're going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:10.000
talk about now, which is firings related to people&nbsp;
who are refusing to get vaccinated for their jobs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.240
as required by their employers. Yesterday, we had&nbsp;
two stories sort of about this one story asked,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:23.200
is it time to start firing unvaccinated employees&nbsp;
and mass, so to speak? That was one question we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:29.440
talked about yesterday. Many of you wrote to me&nbsp;
and said, yeah, it is it once once you say those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:33.760
are the rules, you've got to follow through.&nbsp;
Otherwise, these are empty threats. It's like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:38.240
the parent who makes an empty threat to the kid&nbsp;
or, I don't know, whatever analogy you want.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:43.040
The second question we asked yesterday in another&nbsp;
segment and many of you wrote in about this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:48.560
one as well, is are some of the people saying&nbsp;
they're going to quit over a vaccine mandate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:54.960
lying or exaggerating or maybe even&nbsp;
misunderstanding their own willingness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:59.280
to quit? And they're not really going to&nbsp;
quit. They're probably just going to go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:03.840
and get vaccinated. And one of the examples we&nbsp;
had yesterday was Massachusetts state troopers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:10.640
where the union for the state troopers said we've&nbsp;
gotten dozens and dozens, you know, massive dumps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:17.680
of resignation letters. The unions said that.&nbsp;
But state police, human resources said one one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:24.080
trooper actually resigned. Now we'll see how it&nbsp;
all shakes out. We now have a couple of additional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:31.520
data points. And it seems as though there are&nbsp;
people willing to quit, but more likely be fired&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:37.440
over not getting vaccinated. But yesterday's&nbsp;
assessment that it might only be half to one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:44.480
percent, half of one to one percent of employees&nbsp;
at any given organization may well be right. Let's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:50.160
look at a couple of data points. Washington Post&nbsp;
reporting North Carolina hospital system fires&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:56.880
about one hundred seventy five workers and one&nbsp;
of the largest ever mass terminations due to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:02.160
vaccine mandate. Timothy Bella writes. A North&nbsp;
Carolina based hospital system announced Monday&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:09.760
that roughly 175 unvaccinated employees were fired&nbsp;
for failing to comply with the organization's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:15.600
mandatory covid vaccination policy. The latest in&nbsp;
a series of health care dismissals. We're going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:23.680
to get to that. Novant Health said last week that&nbsp;
375 unvaccinated workers across 15 hospitals and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:29.840
800 clinics had been suspended for not getting&nbsp;
immunized. They were given five days to comply.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:37.520
Novant Health spokeswoman Megan Rivers' tweeted&nbsp;
Monday that almost 200 of the suspended workers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:43.040
received their first dose by Friday. The hospital&nbsp;
confirmed that the rest of the suspended employees&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:49.600
who did not comply were fired, although the exact&nbsp;
number of those dismissed was not specified.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:54.960
We stand by our decision to make the vaccine&nbsp;
mandatory as we have a responsibility to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.960 --> 00:03:00.080
protect our patients, visitors and team members,&nbsp;
regardless of where they are in our health system.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:06.240
We couldn't be prouder of our team members who&nbsp;
made the choice to receive the covid-19 vaccine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:11.680
and remain part of the team. Later, the article&nbsp;
says the mass termination of unvaccinated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:17.120
hospital system employees is among the largest&nbsp;
of its kind to date. More than 150 health care&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:21.760
workers who didn't comply with the mandate. At&nbsp;
Houston Methodist, which was one of the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:28.080
to require the shots, were fired or resigned in&nbsp;
June after a federal judge upheld the policy. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:34.960
importantly. More than 99 percent of&nbsp;
the system's 35000 employees followed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:42.000
the program. We have a few other data points here&nbsp;
as well. Beckers Hospital Review put out yesterday&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:48.320
a sort of summary of departures at 18 different&nbsp;
health systems. Now, departure could be firing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:53.680
or resignation. It could be either. And it&nbsp;
includes St. Luke's University Health Network,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.640 --> 00:04:00.000
17000 employees, about one hundred and&nbsp;
fifty total refused to get vaccinated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:08.160
and resigned. That is just under one percent.&nbsp;
Newark Delawares Christiana Care fired about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:15.760
150, or the equivalent of under 90 full timers&nbsp;
for not complying in New York City, New York,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:26.320
Presbyterian's 48000 team member system had fewer&nbsp;
than two hundred and fifty resignations firings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:30.320
That is about half of one percent right&nbsp;
along with our estimate from yesterday,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:38.400
New Hyde Park, New York's Northwest Health had&nbsp;
about two dozen leaders not allowed to continue.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:43.520
We don't know the total number there. So you can&nbsp;
go and look at the exact numbers here. But what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:51.280
are we learning so far? First and foremost, it&nbsp;
does seem that when there is a disproportionate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:59.120
amount of headlines about people resigning&nbsp;
or people saying, fire me, fire me, sirs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:06.560
that the real number of people willing to go and&nbsp;
whether it's a resignation or a firing, you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:10.960
doesn't really make a difference. It seems that&nbsp;
it's about half of one percent to one percent.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:16.160
That's number one. The second thing here is,&nbsp;
you know, when it comes to health care systems,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:22.960
this is not just about the employer in a vacuum&nbsp;
saying you got to be vaccinated and otherwise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:28.960
you're out with no real connection to reality.&nbsp;
This clearly also has to do with patients.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:36.240
And what they should do is the nurses that don't&nbsp;
want to get vaccinated, the administrators that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:40.400
don't want to impose vaccination. If there are&nbsp;
any the doctors that don't want to get vaccinated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:45.680
they should start their own clinic. They should&nbsp;
start their own hospital. If patients prefer to go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:51.920
and be seen at a place where the employees, nurses&nbsp;
and doctors might be vaccinated or might not. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:57.840
it's not required if that's more appealing to&nbsp;
participants in the health care marketplace,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:02.560
because that's what it is in the United States.&nbsp;
If people would rather go to the place where maybe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:06.560
the employees and service providers, health&nbsp;
providers aren't vaccinated, then that would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:13.680
be a business. Open a clinic and say, hey, if you&nbsp;
want freedom, come be seen here, come to our E.R.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:18.080
We don't make the nurses get vaccinated.&nbsp;
We don't make the doctors get vaccinated.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:25.360
If that's a popular idea in the marketplace of&nbsp;
ideas, then do it and it will be very profitable.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:32.080
My prediction is most people who go to a health&nbsp;
care setting want to go somewhere where they know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:36.720
the people providing care to them have been&nbsp;
vaccinated. But this is a great opportunity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:41.920
to test it. What do you think would happen in that&nbsp;
situation? Let me know. You can find me on Twitter&nbsp;&nbsp;

